>If someone has a spoiler for what to do in the room with an altar
>and priest(ess), please let me know. I've given money to the priest(ess)
>to no avail, and have only sacrificed one dead corpse on the altar
>with no visible effects.

>
(1) Sacrifice more at the altar.  Unless you don't get a
"hopeful feeling" or "feeling of inadequacy" it is safe to pray.
Praying can have excellent side effects.  Be patient.  There are
also benefits to performing sacrifices and not praying.

(2) The priest(ess) is carrying 3 spellbooks, a cloak of protection,
and other decent stuff.  If you have *no* money try #chatting with the
priest just for fun.  If you have a ring of conflict, you can make the
priest fight all sorts of things and kill them for you.  Then you can
sacrifice the corpses.  If you can get the priest between you and a
dragon then the priest will eventually be toasted and you can take the
priest's stuff (assuming that you are far enough along so that you can
survive the dragon yourself).

>As to why you would want to put things in a chest:
>Maybe you are on a level with an altar. You want to do mass offerings,
>so you wait 50-100 turns. Kill some orcs. Sacrifice some orcs. But now
>there's orc scimitars and knives all around the place. Rather than waiting
>for monsters to pick them up and hit you with them, you would put them in
>the box. :)
>
Someone earlier asked how to get rid of stuff.  Before filling the
chest try dipping it in unholy water.  After filling the chest, try
taking the stuff out.  I haven't actually tried this with chests but
only with cursed bags.


